@* The app boundary's error content, so this renders in place of the entire app - the router, the layout and
   the MudThemeProvider with it. Plain HTML and pinned colors for that reason: with the theme provider gone
   so are the --mud-palette variables every MudBlazor component draws itself from. app.css is a stylesheet
   index.html loads, so it is still here, and .fatal-error in it pins what this needs. *@
<div class="fatal-error">
    <div class="fatal-error-panel">
        <h1 class="fatal-error-title display-title">Crafting Calculator ran into a problem</h1>
        <p class="fatal-error-body">
            Your data is fine. Whatever the problem is, it's been written to the log file.
        </p>
        <p class="fatal-error-body fatal-error-hint">
            Try again picks up where you left off. Restart reloads the app.
        </p>
        <div class="fatal-error-actions">
            <button type="button" class="fatal-error-button" @onclick="TryAgain">Try again</button>
            <button type="button" class="fatal-error-button fatal-error-button-quiet" @onclick="Restart">Restart</button>
        </div>
    </div>
</div>
